1
00:00:03,712 --> 00:00:05,380
Boy, do I have to urinate.

2
00:00:06,924 --> 00:00:08,967
If only there were a solution
to that.

3
00:00:10,260 --> 00:00:13,138
Seriously. I feel like I've got
a fish tank in my pelvis.

4
00:00:15,140 --> 00:00:16,475
So go to the bathroom.

5
00:00:16,683 --> 00:00:17,851
I can't.

6
00:00:18,143 --> 00:00:19,520
Why not?

7
00:00:19,978 --> 00:00:24,483
Because I'm trying to decide
between getting an Xbox One or a PS4.

8
00:00:25,734 --> 00:00:27,945
Oh, "pee." Why'd I say that?

9
00:00:30,739 --> 00:00:32,574
Forgive me for asking
a stupid question,

10
00:00:32,783 --> 00:00:34,451
but why are you being stupid?

11
00:00:35,911 --> 00:00:37,287
I'm not being stupid.

12
00:00:37,496 --> 00:00:40,374
I'm employing the work
of Dutch researcher, Mirjam Tuk,

13
00:00:40,582 --> 00:00:43,460
who found that people with full
bladders make better decisions.

14
00:00:44,795 --> 00:00:47,839
Why did I pee before I decided
to move in here?

15
00:00:48,590 --> 00:00:49,633
(DOOR OPENS)

16
00:00:49,841 --> 00:00:51,885
-Hi!
-Hey. How'd the audition go?

17
00:00:52,135 --> 00:00:54,888
I killed it. I was even able
to cry real tears right on the spot.

18
00:00:55,097 --> 00:00:56,181
-That's great.
-I know.

19
00:00:56,390 --> 00:00:57,975
Next time I get pulled over
for a speeding ticket,

20
00:00:58,183 --> 00:00:59,601
here come the waterworks.

21
00:01:00,018 --> 00:01:01,603
Here come the waterworks!

22
00:01:03,480 --> 00:01:04,523
(DOOR CLOSES)

23
00:01:06,984 --> 00:01:09,278
-Aren't you gonna ask?
-What is this, my first day?

24
00:01:10,404 --> 00:01:12,281
(THEME SONG PLAYS)

25
00:01:35,304 --> 00:01:37,514
Can I get your opinion on something
that happened at work today?

26
00:01:37,681 --> 00:01:38,724
-Yeah, sure.
-Of course.

27
00:01:38,890 --> 00:01:42,101
I did something that will either
make me look like a lovable goof

28
00:01:42,269 --> 00:01:43,520
The Indecision Amalgamation

29
00:01:43,687 --> 00:01:46,565
or a horrible monster damned
to spend eternity in hell.

30
00:01:47,608 --> 00:01:48,692
I'm sure it's lovable.

31
00:01:48,900 --> 00:01:50,861
I'm gonna go with monster.
What do you got?

32
00:01:52,279 --> 00:01:54,281
Well, there's this lady
in our office who's retiring,

33
00:01:54,489 --> 00:01:56,825
and they were passing around one of
those big cards for us to sign...

34
00:01:57,034 --> 00:01:58,076
Okay.

35
00:01:58,285 --> 00:02:01,580
No one told me she was in a horrible
car accident over the weekend

36
00:02:01,788 --> 00:02:03,957
and what I was signing
was not a retirement card

37
00:02:04,166 --> 00:02:05,876
but was actually a "get well" card.

38
00:02:06,084 --> 00:02:08,670
(CHUCKLING)
I'm liking my odds here.

39
00:02:10,130 --> 00:02:12,549
So on the card, in the hospital,

40
00:02:12,758 --> 00:02:15,427
next to the woman who's clinging
to life are the words,

41
00:02:15,636 --> 00:02:17,763
"Hey, Vivian. You deserve this.

42
00:02:21,933 --> 00:02:23,435
And at least with you gone,

43
00:02:23,644 --> 00:02:25,395
no one will steal my yogurt
out of the fridge."

44
00:02:25,604 --> 00:02:27,230
No!

45
00:02:29,524 --> 00:02:30,692
"LOL. Smiley face."

46
00:02:30,901 --> 00:02:32,778
Oh, my gosh.

47
00:02:33,528 --> 00:02:35,280
"P.S.
Good luck wherever you wind up."

48
00:02:37,407 --> 00:02:39,618
Why didn't I put money on this?

49
00:02:40,994 --> 00:02:42,037
(PHONE CHIMING)

50
00:02:42,245 --> 00:02:43,705
Hey, that's my agent.
If I got the part,

51
00:02:43,914 --> 00:02:47,084
it's still the second best thing
I've heard all day. Hello?

52
00:02:47,501 --> 00:02:48,752
Am I a terrible person?

53
00:02:48,960 --> 00:02:51,338
No. No, it was a mistake.

54
00:02:51,546 --> 00:02:53,048
Am I a terrible person
that it crossed my mind

55
00:02:53,256 --> 00:02:55,133
that she might die
and never see the card?

56
00:02:55,550 --> 00:02:57,552
Now I think you're flirting
with the line.

57
00:02:58,970 --> 00:03:00,972
-Good news?
-No, I didn't get it.

58
00:03:01,180 --> 00:03:02,391
I'm so sorry.

59
00:03:02,599 --> 00:03:04,183
You'll get offered something soon.

60
00:03:04,393 --> 00:03:06,645
I kind of did. The part
in that awful horror movie

61
00:03:06,853 --> 00:03:08,313
I passed on came back around.

62
00:03:08,522 --> 00:03:10,232
Apparently, it's mine if I want it.

63
00:03:10,440 --> 00:03:11,525
Are you gonna take it?

64
00:03:11,733 --> 00:03:13,068
I don't know what to do.

65
00:03:13,276 --> 00:03:15,194
Maybe you'll get hit
by a car and die.

66
00:03:18,490 --> 00:03:19,658
LOL, right?

67
00:03:26,915 --> 00:03:28,458
Hey. Emily, right?

68
00:03:29,292 --> 00:03:30,335
Yeah.

69
00:03:30,544 --> 00:03:32,754
I don't know if you remember me.

70
00:03:32,963 --> 00:03:34,589
From the dating website.

71
00:03:34,798 --> 00:03:36,967
Your friend emailed me
because you were afraid to,

72
00:03:37,175 --> 00:03:38,885
then you tracked me down
and acted like a lunatic?

73
00:03:39,094 --> 00:03:41,012
Yes, Rajesh Koothrappali.

74
00:03:42,556 --> 00:03:45,726
Look, I just...
I wanted to say I'm sorry.

75
00:03:46,768 --> 00:03:49,396
You were, like, the coolest person
I ever found online,

76
00:03:49,604 --> 00:03:53,400
and I got really nervous
and I just blew it.

77
00:03:54,443 --> 00:03:55,569
Don't worry about it.

78
00:03:56,403 --> 00:03:57,904
And if it makes you feel any better,

79
00:03:58,113 --> 00:04:00,365
you're not the weirdest guy
I've met off the Internet.

80
00:04:00,574 --> 00:04:04,077
Well, give me a chance,
you don't even know me.

81
00:04:06,455 --> 00:04:09,249
All right, here's your chance.

82
00:04:09,708 --> 00:04:11,460
What? Really?

83
00:04:12,544 --> 00:04:13,670
Thank you.

84
00:04:13,879 --> 00:04:15,297
Fate has given me
a rare second chance,

85
00:04:15,505 --> 00:04:17,299
and I swear to Vishnu
I'm not gonna blow it.

86
00:04:18,675 --> 00:04:20,927
Or normal words
followed by a charming smile.

87
00:04:26,641 --> 00:04:29,186
First there was PlayStation,
aka PS1,

88
00:04:29,394 --> 00:04:32,355
then PS2, PS3 and now PS4.

89
00:04:32,564 --> 00:04:33,648
And that makes sense.

90
00:04:33,857 --> 00:04:36,318
You'd think after Xbox,
there'd be Xbox 2.

91
00:04:36,526 --> 00:04:40,238
But no, next came Xbox 360. Hm?

92
00:04:40,447 --> 00:04:43,450
And now, after 360, comes Xbox One.

93
00:04:44,910 --> 00:04:45,952
Why "One"?

94
00:04:46,870 --> 00:04:49,289
Maybe that's how many seconds
of thought they put into naming it.

95
00:04:50,624 --> 00:04:51,875
Can you get the butter, please?

96
00:04:52,083 --> 00:04:54,669
You know, however,
with the Xbox One,

97
00:04:54,878 --> 00:04:57,088
I can control
my entire entertainment system

98
00:04:57,296 --> 00:04:58,673
using voice commands.

99
00:04:58,882 --> 00:05:00,884
Up until now,
I've had to use Leonard.

100
00:05:02,677 --> 00:05:04,679
Then get the other one.
Pass the butter.

101
00:05:05,263 --> 00:05:06,765
Hang on.

102
00:05:06,973 --> 00:05:09,518
I don't feel like you're taking
this dilemma seriously.

103
00:05:10,936 --> 00:05:12,312
Fine, Sheldon.

104
00:05:12,729 --> 00:05:14,231
You have my undivided attention.

105
00:05:14,481 --> 00:05:18,902
Okay, now, the PS4 is
more angular and sleek-looking.

106
00:05:19,110 --> 00:05:20,987
-(MOCKING) No way.
-Yeah.

107
00:05:21,196 --> 00:05:24,074
It's true. But the larger size
of the Xbox One

108
00:05:24,282 --> 00:05:25,534
may keep it from overheating.

109
00:05:25,742 --> 00:05:27,953
You wouldn't want
your gaming system to overheat.

110
00:05:28,161 --> 00:05:29,996
Well, you absolutely would not.

111
00:05:30,205 --> 00:05:33,875
And furthermore, the Xbox One
now comes with a Kinect included.

112
00:05:34,084 --> 00:05:35,961
-Included?
-Yes!

113
00:05:37,045 --> 00:05:38,505
Not sold separately.

114
00:05:38,713 --> 00:05:42,968
Although, the PS4
uses cool new GDDR5 RAM,

115
00:05:43,176 --> 00:05:46,179
while the Xbox One is still using
the conventional DDR3 memory.

116
00:05:46,388 --> 00:05:48,181
Why would they still
be using DDR3?

117
00:05:48,390 --> 00:05:49,891
Are they nuts?

118
00:05:51,726 --> 00:05:52,978
See? That's what I thought.

119
00:05:53,186 --> 00:05:55,647
But then they go and throw in
an ESRAM buffer.

120
00:05:55,856 --> 00:05:58,900
-Whoa. Wait a second. Who's "they"?
-Xbox.

121
00:05:59,109 --> 00:06:01,528
-You're kidding!
-No, I am not!

122
00:06:01,736 --> 00:06:03,864
And this ESRAM buffer
should totally bridge

123
00:06:04,072 --> 00:06:05,699
the 100-gigabit-per-second
bandwidth gap

124
00:06:05,907 --> 00:06:06,992
between the two RAM types.

125
00:06:07,200 --> 00:06:09,536
This is a nightmare.
How will you ever make a decision?

126
00:06:09,744 --> 00:06:11,746
I don't know!
What should I do?

127
00:06:11,955 --> 00:06:13,790
Please pass the butter!

128
00:06:24,426 --> 00:06:26,720
Okay, it's not me, right?
This script is terrible.

129
00:06:26,928 --> 00:06:28,221
Yeah.

130
00:06:29,306 --> 00:06:31,099
I had higher hopes for a movie called

131
00:06:31,308 --> 00:06:34,311
Serial Ape-ist 2:
Monkey See, Monkey Kill.

132
00:06:37,522 --> 00:06:40,525
You know, it's still possible
for you to be good in a bad movie.

133
00:06:40,734 --> 00:06:42,068
Okay.
(CLEARS THROAT)

134
00:06:44,029 --> 00:06:45,739
"Sometimes I feel like I can control

135
00:06:45,947 --> 00:06:47,741
the killer gorilla instinct
inside of me,

136
00:06:47,949 --> 00:06:49,701
but then I see these bananas

137
00:06:49,910 --> 00:06:52,829
and I just want to eat them
and then kill people."

138
00:06:57,000 --> 00:06:58,376
What am I gonna do?

139
00:06:58,585 --> 00:07:01,963
Well, for starters,
I wouldn't eat the bananas.

140
00:07:02,714 --> 00:07:04,674
Come on! This is serious.

141
00:07:04,883 --> 00:07:06,927
(STAMMERING)
Does it at least pay well?

142
00:07:07,135 --> 00:07:09,179
Less than I was making
at The Cheesecake Factory.

143
00:07:09,554 --> 00:07:10,639
What does your agent think?

144
00:07:10,847 --> 00:07:13,183
She's thinking of taking a job
at The Cheesecake Factory.

145
00:07:15,727 --> 00:07:17,354
You know what,
why don't you just do it?

146
00:07:17,562 --> 00:07:19,856
You'll go have fun for a few weeks,
make some money,

147
00:07:20,065 --> 00:07:21,942
and who knows what it might lead to?

148
00:07:22,150 --> 00:07:23,360
Okay, look, here, page 58.

149
00:07:23,568 --> 00:07:26,112
I oil-wrestle an orangutan
in a bikini.

150
00:07:27,572 --> 00:07:30,533
Just to clarify, which one
of you is wearing the bikini?

151
00:07:31,576 --> 00:07:33,244
Both of us.

152
00:07:34,746 --> 00:07:36,331
So it's a family film.

153
00:07:39,918 --> 00:07:41,544
Thank you again for dinner.

154
00:07:41,753 --> 00:07:42,796
You're welcome.

155
00:07:43,004 --> 00:07:46,299
-Good night.
-Uh, it's date night.

156
00:07:46,508 --> 00:07:49,135
Aren't you forgetting something?

157
00:07:50,469 --> 00:07:51,930
Oh, of course.

158
00:07:59,270 --> 00:08:02,148
Did I mention
the PS4 controllers light up?

159
00:08:05,318 --> 00:08:06,653
No.

160
00:08:07,237 --> 00:08:08,655
Well, they do.

161
00:08:13,326 --> 00:08:15,245
And then after coffee,
we went for a walk

162
00:08:15,453 --> 00:08:17,288
and she told me she always
thought people from India

163
00:08:17,496 --> 00:08:18,957
were exotic and mysterious.

164
00:08:19,165 --> 00:08:21,876
So, with my mouth, I said,
"We're just like anybody else,"

165
00:08:22,085 --> 00:08:23,545
but with my eyes, I said,

166
00:08:23,753 --> 00:08:25,839
"Straight up, Red,
hop on my flying carpet."

167
00:08:29,467 --> 00:08:30,760
So, you gonna see her again?

168
00:08:30,969 --> 00:08:32,053
Yeah, we have plans this weekend.

169
00:08:32,262 --> 00:08:33,304
And if it's a clear night,

170
00:08:33,512 --> 00:08:36,391
I'm gonna lay
some romantic astronomy on her.

171
00:08:37,892 --> 00:08:39,060
Okay, like what? Show me.

172
00:08:39,269 --> 00:08:40,729
I can't do that to Leonard.

173
00:08:40,937 --> 00:08:43,273
This is some powerful
panty-dropping stuff.

174
00:08:46,067 --> 00:08:48,486
You have my blessing. Go for it.

175
00:08:49,112 --> 00:08:50,488
Okay.
(CLEARS THROAT)

176
00:08:52,365 --> 00:08:57,162
Penny, two of the brightest stars
in the night sky

177
00:08:57,370 --> 00:08:59,622
are Altair and Vega.

178
00:08:59,831 --> 00:09:02,125
And it is said
they were deeply in love

179
00:09:02,333 --> 00:09:06,629
but forever separated by the
celestial river of the Milky Way.

180
00:09:07,213 --> 00:09:08,590
-That's sad.
-It is.

181
00:09:08,798 --> 00:09:11,051
But once a year,

182
00:09:11,259 --> 00:09:13,845
on the seventh day
of the seventh month,

183
00:09:14,054 --> 00:09:18,391
Vega cries so hard that all
the magpies in the world fly up

184
00:09:18,600 --> 00:09:22,937
and create a bridge with their wings
so the two lovers can be together

185
00:09:23,146 --> 00:09:25,982
for a single night of passion.

186
00:09:27,650 --> 00:09:28,985
Wow.

187
00:09:32,113 --> 00:09:33,448
Okay, that's enough.

188
00:09:37,160 --> 00:09:40,830
Quick poll: PS4 or Xbox One?
Raj.

189
00:09:41,039 --> 00:09:42,082
-Xbox One.
-Penny.

190
00:09:42,290 --> 00:09:43,333
Huh?

191
00:09:44,292 --> 00:09:45,584
-Leonard.
-PS4.

192
00:09:45,794 --> 00:09:47,504
-Wolowitz.
-Both great.

193
00:09:47,712 --> 00:09:49,631
-Bernadette.
-I like the Wii.

194
00:09:52,675 --> 00:09:54,135
Thanks, Grandma.

195
00:09:57,013 --> 00:09:58,598
-Oh, my goodness.
-What's up?

196
00:09:58,807 --> 00:10:01,267
I just got an email
from my ex-girlfriend Lucy.

197
00:10:01,476 --> 00:10:04,020
She misses me
and wants to get together.

198
00:10:04,229 --> 00:10:07,982
Two women at the same time?
Nice job, playa!

199
00:10:10,360 --> 00:10:11,486
Really?

200
00:10:12,862 --> 00:10:15,865
Was it the "two women"
thing or the "playa"?

201
00:10:17,367 --> 00:10:19,077
It was the "playa".

202
00:10:22,664 --> 00:10:23,832
What am I supposed to do?

203
00:10:24,040 --> 00:10:26,709
How am I supposed to choose
between Emily and Lucy?

204
00:10:26,918 --> 00:10:29,003
Why do you have to choose?
Date both of them.

205
00:10:29,212 --> 00:10:31,256
I can't date two women at once.

206
00:10:31,464 --> 00:10:33,508
Zero women, that's my sweet spot.

207
00:10:35,426 --> 00:10:36,719
Unless you're sleeping
with one of them,

208
00:10:36,928 --> 00:10:38,388
seeing other people isn't a big deal.

209
00:10:38,596 --> 00:10:41,349
But what if one of them asks me
what I was up to the night before

210
00:10:41,558 --> 00:10:44,310
and I was with the other one?
Then, what, do I lie?

211
00:10:44,519 --> 00:10:46,271
-Yes.
-Yes.

212
00:10:48,815 --> 00:10:49,858
What do you mean, yes?

213
00:10:50,066 --> 00:10:51,526
What do you mean, yes?

214
00:10:51,734 --> 00:10:53,778
Were you seeing other women
when we started dating?

215
00:10:53,987 --> 00:10:55,446
No. Were you seeing other men?

216
00:10:55,655 --> 00:10:56,781
No.

217
00:10:56,990 --> 00:10:58,032
Were you seeing other men?

218
00:10:58,241 --> 00:10:59,492
No.

219
00:11:05,039 --> 00:11:06,624
Aren't you gonna ask me?

220
00:11:09,002 --> 00:11:10,587
Come on, really?

221
00:11:13,965 --> 00:11:15,842
Thank you so much
for letting us pick your brain.

222
00:11:16,050 --> 00:11:18,136
Yeah, happy to help.
So, what's going on?

223
00:11:18,344 --> 00:11:21,181
Well, I'm having an impossible time
getting my career off the ground,

224
00:11:21,389 --> 00:11:23,516
and I got offered a role
in this crappy horror movie,

225
00:11:23,725 --> 00:11:25,185
and I just don't know
if I should take it.

226
00:11:25,768 --> 00:11:28,813
Well, I have certainly taken some
jobs that I've been embarrassed by.

227
00:11:29,022 --> 00:11:31,690
I wouldn't exactly call
Star Trek embarrassing.

228
00:11:34,068 --> 00:11:35,528
I wasn't.

229
00:11:37,989 --> 00:11:39,407
Me, either.

230
00:11:41,034 --> 00:11:44,370
So, what do you think, is there a
professional downside to doing it?

231
00:11:44,579 --> 00:11:45,872
Well, it's tricky.

232
00:11:46,080 --> 00:11:48,707
You want to take projects
that you're excited about,

233
00:11:48,917 --> 00:11:51,211
but sometimes you also
have to pay the bills.

234
00:11:52,128 --> 00:11:53,796
When you're on the set
working on something

235
00:11:54,005 --> 00:11:57,342
that you just know in your heart
is bad, not Star Trek...

236
00:11:59,052 --> 00:12:01,346
Yeah, beam me up. I love it!

237
00:12:03,806 --> 00:12:07,101
Anyway, those jobs
can be soul-crushing.

238
00:12:07,310 --> 00:12:08,978
That's what I'm afraid of.

239
00:12:09,187 --> 00:12:11,022
Well, I was in Stand By Me
when I was a kid,

240
00:12:11,231 --> 00:12:12,690
and it was a huge success.

241
00:12:12,899 --> 00:12:15,443
The terrible movies I did
came after that.

242
00:12:15,652 --> 00:12:17,278
Imagine how that feels.

243
00:12:17,487 --> 00:12:18,529
Sounds rough.

244
00:12:18,737 --> 00:12:20,865
I'm telling you,
this business is brutal.

245
00:12:21,074 --> 00:12:24,077
To this day,
I hate going on auditions.

246
00:12:24,285 --> 00:12:28,623
Okay, I walk in, and I can just
feel them thinking,

247
00:12:28,831 --> 00:12:31,918
"He was such a cute kid.
What happened to him?"

248
00:12:34,545 --> 00:12:38,383
And then I don't get the job,
and I can never find out why.

249
00:12:39,968 --> 00:12:42,512
Honestly, I get so depressed,
there are entire weeks

250
00:12:42,720 --> 00:12:45,014
that I can't even get out of bed.

251
00:12:48,142 --> 00:12:49,519
Okay, this was helpful.

252
00:12:53,731 --> 00:12:55,984
Any news on your co-worker
who's in the hospital?

253
00:12:56,192 --> 00:12:59,112
Poor thing,
she was in surgery for 18 hours.

254
00:12:59,320 --> 00:13:01,322
She's alive, but she's
still in critical condition.

255
00:13:01,531 --> 00:13:02,615
Oh, no.

256
00:13:02,824 --> 00:13:04,117
The one bit of good news
is they put her

257
00:13:04,325 --> 00:13:06,327
in a medically induced coma
before she read the card.

258
00:13:06,536 --> 00:13:08,579
So, you know, silver linings.

259
00:13:12,250 --> 00:13:14,335
Were you like this
when I married you?

260
00:13:17,630 --> 00:13:19,424
Don't worry about it, buddy.

261
00:13:19,632 --> 00:13:21,718
-Okay, bye.
-(PHONE BEEPS)

262
00:13:21,926 --> 00:13:23,428
That was Wil,
he's feeling a lot better.

263
00:13:23,636 --> 00:13:26,848
Apparently, he's 12-down
in the TV Guide crossword puzzle.

264
00:13:28,807 --> 00:13:30,643
Did he help you make a decision
about the movie?

265
00:13:30,852 --> 00:13:33,730
No. Did you figure out what you're
gonna do about the two girls?

266
00:13:33,938 --> 00:13:35,398
As a matter of fact, I did.

267
00:13:35,606 --> 00:13:38,234
I've spent so many years
living in fear,

268
00:13:38,443 --> 00:13:40,987
saying no to new experiences,
but from now on,

269
00:13:41,195 --> 00:13:43,281
I'm gonna say yes.
Yes to love,

270
00:13:43,489 --> 00:13:45,325
yes to adventure, yes to life.
Whatever it may be,

271
00:13:45,533 --> 00:13:47,076
the answer's going to be yes.

272
00:13:48,494 --> 00:13:49,537
He's gonna die alone, right?

273
00:13:49,746 --> 00:13:51,205
-Yeah.
-Yes.

274
00:13:54,167 --> 00:13:55,418
I'm proud of you, Sheldon.

275
00:13:55,626 --> 00:13:57,086
You know, I'm proud of me, too.

276
00:13:57,295 --> 00:14:00,590
I've done all my research,
I conducted an informal poll,

277
00:14:00,798 --> 00:14:02,467
and I've arrived
at the rock-solid certainty

278
00:14:02,675 --> 00:14:03,801
I've made the right choice.

279
00:14:04,010 --> 00:14:05,303
Well, that's got to be
a good feeling.

280
00:14:05,511 --> 00:14:06,845
Oh, it is.

281
00:14:07,055 --> 00:14:08,847
-Although--
-Oh, crap.

282
00:14:10,641 --> 00:14:13,811
I had the same feeling when
I made my dad buy a Betamax

283
00:14:14,020 --> 00:14:15,688
instead of a VHS.

284
00:14:16,022 --> 00:14:17,648
You were just a little kid.

285
00:14:17,856 --> 00:14:19,150
A little kid
who picked the wrong format

286
00:14:19,359 --> 00:14:21,235
to record The MacNeil/Lehrer Report.

287
00:14:23,321 --> 00:14:27,450
I also was certain that HD DVD
would win out over Blu-ray.

288
00:14:27,658 --> 00:14:29,702
-How old were you then?
-Old enough to know better.

289
00:14:31,871 --> 00:14:35,083
And now that I think about it,
I stood in front of a case of iPods

290
00:14:35,291 --> 00:14:37,001
and I bought a Zune.

291
00:14:40,463 --> 00:14:41,547
What's a Zune?

292
00:14:41,756 --> 00:14:43,383
Yeah, exactly.

293
00:14:44,926 --> 00:14:48,096
It's an MP3 player
brought to us by the makers of Xbox.

294
00:14:49,430 --> 00:14:51,516
No, what are you doing?
No, pick that back up.

295
00:14:51,724 --> 00:14:53,643
You know it's good.
You did the research.

296
00:14:53,851 --> 00:14:55,186
But what if I'm wrong?

297
00:14:56,104 --> 00:14:59,107
You know what?
How about I buy it for you?

298
00:14:59,315 --> 00:15:01,609
How about I buy you both?

299
00:15:02,443 --> 00:15:04,153
You know I only have
one slot available

300
00:15:04,362 --> 00:15:05,530
on my entertainment center.

301
00:15:05,738 --> 00:15:07,573
Then I'll buy you
a new entertainment center.

302
00:15:07,782 --> 00:15:10,618
Yeah, okay, sure.
But which one?

303
00:15:12,745 --> 00:15:16,082
How about this?
I've heard that if you flip a coin,

304
00:15:16,290 --> 00:15:17,916
it will tell you how
you actually feel.

305
00:15:18,126 --> 00:15:19,502
Because you'll either
be disappointed

306
00:15:19,710 --> 00:15:21,337
or excited by the outcome.

307
00:15:21,546 --> 00:15:22,588
Interesting.

308
00:15:22,797 --> 00:15:26,008
So, heads it's PS4,
tails it's Xbox One.

309
00:15:27,510 --> 00:15:29,011
All right, I'll try.

310
00:15:33,391 --> 00:15:34,559
What is it?

311
00:15:34,892 --> 00:15:36,310
A quarter.

312
00:15:40,356 --> 00:15:42,525
Could have given it back to me.
That was a choice.

313
00:15:48,072 --> 00:15:49,115
(SIGHS)

314
00:15:50,867 --> 00:15:52,827
You look really pretty tonight.

315
00:15:53,035 --> 00:15:55,204
Thanks. I love that jacket.

316
00:15:55,413 --> 00:15:56,955
Thank you. Thanks.

317
00:16:00,209 --> 00:16:01,711
I'm sorry. I can't do this.

318
00:16:01,919 --> 00:16:04,964
My ex-girlfriend emailed me,
and I'm seeing her Saturday.

319
00:16:05,173 --> 00:16:07,550
And I'm glad you like it,
it's from J. Crew.

320
00:16:09,886 --> 00:16:11,095
I don't understand.

321
00:16:11,304 --> 00:16:13,764
My friends told me it was okay to see
more than one person at a time,

322
00:16:13,973 --> 00:16:16,517
but it feels like
I'm being deceitful.

323
00:16:16,726 --> 00:16:18,269
Are you getting
back together with her?

324
00:16:19,353 --> 00:16:22,773
No. I have no idea.
What would you do?

325
00:16:23,900 --> 00:16:26,903
Usually on first dates,
I talk about music and stuff,

326
00:16:27,111 --> 00:16:28,529
but I was promised weird,
so let's do this.

327
00:16:31,282 --> 00:16:32,783
How serious were you two?

328
00:16:33,493 --> 00:16:35,119
Well, to be honest,

329
00:16:35,328 --> 00:16:38,498
we only went on four dates,
hugged twice, kissed once,

330
00:16:38,706 --> 00:16:41,709
and there was a handshake
loaded with sexual innuendo.

331
00:16:45,421 --> 00:16:49,133
Wait, a girl you never slept with
sent you an email

332
00:16:49,342 --> 00:16:51,928
and you felt so guilty about it
that you had to tell me?

333
00:16:52,136 --> 00:16:53,513
Yeah.

334
00:16:53,721 --> 00:16:55,097
That's kind of adorable.

335
00:16:56,265 --> 00:16:58,976
Are you sure?
Because this is the part of the night

336
00:16:59,185 --> 00:17:01,479
where I've said something stupid
and the girl usually leaves.

337
00:17:01,687 --> 00:17:03,147
I'm still here.

338
00:17:03,356 --> 00:17:05,900
Yeah, but now you make me wonder
what's wrong with you.

339
00:17:08,236 --> 00:17:09,529
We just met.

340
00:17:09,737 --> 00:17:12,198
You don't need to tell me about
other people you're seeing.

341
00:17:12,740 --> 00:17:14,116
Really?

342
00:17:14,325 --> 00:17:15,952
Because "I'm dating two women"

343
00:17:16,160 --> 00:17:19,413
is basically the only cool thing
I can say about myself.

344
00:17:20,831 --> 00:17:22,333
(BOTH LAUGHING)

345
00:17:30,716 --> 00:17:34,136
On the one hand, the Xbox One
has a better camera,

346
00:17:34,345 --> 00:17:36,973
but the PS4 has
a removable hard drive.

347
00:17:38,182 --> 00:17:39,517
Thoughts?

348
00:17:40,768 --> 00:17:42,395
I can't feel my legs.

349
00:17:45,147 --> 00:17:46,190
Oh...

350
00:17:46,399 --> 00:17:48,568
I'm sorry, guys, but the store
closed five minutes ago.

351
00:17:49,527 --> 00:17:51,112
But I haven't decided yet.

352
00:17:51,320 --> 00:17:53,781
You'll have to come back tomorrow.
The registers are closed.

353
00:17:55,825 --> 00:17:57,243
(SOBBING)

354
00:17:58,494 --> 00:18:01,539
Let's get you some food.
You'll feel better after you eat.

355
00:18:01,747 --> 00:18:03,457
Okay.

356
00:18:03,666 --> 00:18:07,503
What do you want like, Thai food?
A burger?

357
00:18:07,712 --> 00:18:09,672
(SCREAMING)
I don't know!

358
00:18:20,558 --> 00:18:22,393
SHELDON: Hey, look, a quarter!

359
00:18:31,319 --> 00:18:32,361
How's that feel?

360
00:18:32,570 --> 00:18:34,822
Great.
Not like regret at all.

361
00:18:38,242 --> 00:18:39,577
Penny?

362
00:18:40,244 --> 00:18:41,287
We're working together!

363
00:18:42,997 --> 00:18:44,040
Awesome!

